        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f717f6cf-c240-5760-bdad-c2a4c3d873cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fetteresso Castle, Cowie Castle, Catterline, Aberdeenshire, Scotland, Glasgow\n- People: Joan Eardley\n- Buildings: Fiddes Castle, Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, Muchalls Castle\n- Topics: architecture, historic features, art\n\nFacts:\n- Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse.\n- Fetteresso Castle was rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish Gothic-style Palladian manor.\n- The site of Fetteresso Castle shows clear evidence of prehistoric use.\n- Cowie Castle is a ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.\n- The general area around Catterline includes notable architectural or historic features such as Fetteresso Castle, Fiddes Castle, the Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, and Muchalls Castle.\n- Joan Kathleen Harding Eardley was born on 18 May 1921 and died on 16 August 1963.\n- Joan Eardley was a British artist noted for portraiture of street children in Glasgow.\n- Joan Eardley was also noted for landscapes of the fishing village of Catterline and its surroundings on the north-east coast of Scotland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
